","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Planning service shows 2.2% overspend, the highest percentage variance across services","lead":"Concentrated overspends in individual services may indicate management control issues or unexpected cost drivers that could spread to other areas","iso":"2026-09-29","paper_title":"FINANCE REPORT - App 1 - Revenue Budget Summary","paper_url":"https://moderngov.denbighshire.gov.uk/documents/s67398/67398.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"FINANCE REPORT - App 1 - Revenue Budget Summary","paper_url":"https://moderngov.denbighshire.gov.uk/documents/s67398/67398.pdf","headline":"Corporate income projections slashed by \u00a328.2m from budgeted \u00a329.3m to \u00a31.1m","detail":"Corporate income is now forecast at only \u00a31,077k compared to budgeted \u00a329,271k, a shortfall of \u00a328,194k. This is offset by equivalent expenditure cuts, keeping net position neutral, but the scale of income reduction is extraordinary.","category":"income","matters":"A \u00a328m drop in corporate income expectations signals either loss of expected revenue sources or major budget reclassification; either way, it indicates the council's income base is less stable than budgeted","figures":"\u00a328,194k reduction in income (from \u00a329,271k to \u00a31,077k)","quote":"Corporate 53,986 -29,271 24,715 25,792 -1,077 24,715 -28,194 28,194 0 0.0%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"FINANCE REPORT - App 1 - Revenue Budget Summary","paper_url":"https://moderngov.denbighshire.gov.uk/documents/s67398/67398.pdf","headline":"Adult Social Care overspending by \u00a3442k on the council's largest service budget","detail":"Adult Social Care and Homelessness, budgeted at \u00a367,754k (the largest service budget), is forecast to overspend by \u00a3442k (0.7%). This is the largest absolute overspend in the services section.","category":"overspend","matters":"ASC is nationally a growing cost area; overspends here are significant given budget size and reflect sector-wide demand pressures that raise questions about future financial sustainability","figures":"\u00a3442k overspend (0.7%) on \u00a367,754k budget","quote":"Adult Social Care and Homelessness 89,950 -22,638 67,312 83,008 -15,254 67,754 -6,942 7,384 442 0.7% 0","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"FINANCE REPORT - App 1 - Revenue Budget Summary","paper_url":"https://moderngov.denbighshire.gov.uk/documents/s67398/67398.pdf","headline":"Planning service shows 2.2% overspend, the highest percentage variance across services","detail":"Planning, Public Protection and Countryside services are forecast to overspend by \u00a3268k against a budget of \u00a312,213k. This is the largest percentage variance in the services section and points to specific cost pressures.","category":"overspend","matters":"Concentrated overspends in individual services may indicate management control issues or unexpected cost drivers that could spread to other areas","figures":"\u00a3268k overspend (2.2%) on \u00a312,213k budget","quote":"Planning, Public Protection and Countryside 20,762 -8,549 12,213 18,291 -5,810 12,481 -2,471 2,739 268 2.2% 286","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"FINANCE REPORT - App 1 - Revenue Budget Summary","paper_url":"https://moderngov.denbighshire.gov.uk/documents/s67398/67398.pdf","headline":"Council budget overspend of \u00a3510k worsens from previous forecast of \u00a3108k","detail":"Projected Council Budget outturn is \u00a3309,415k against budget of \u00a3308,905k, a \u00a3510k overspend (0.2%). This represents a deterioration of \u00a3402k from the previous position. The position is getting worse, not better.","category":"overspend","matters":"A lender needs to understand trajectory\u2014a deteriorating position suggests budget control is slipping and may require drawing on reserves or immediate corrective action","figures":"\u00a3510k overspend against \u00a3309m budget (0.2%), versus \u00a3108k previous","quote":"Total Council Budget 419,471 -110,566 308,905 366,835 -57,420 309,415 -52,636 53,146 510 0.2% 108","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-03","committee":"Communities Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A - Waste and Recycling Budget and Costs - July 2026","paper_url":"https://moderngov.denbighshire.gov.uk/documents/s67002/67002.pdf","headline":"First full year (2025/26) balanced budget rests on \u00a32m Extended Producer Responsibility grant described as uncertain","detail":"Service reported balanced budget at 2025/26 year-end: actual costs \u00a38.678m against budget \u00a38.7m. This required \u00a32m pEPR grant funding (out of \u00a32.4m received; \u00a30.4m set aside in reserve). Without grant, costs would have been \u00a310.7m. Council acknowledges future pEPR funding levels are uncertain and whether it will impact Welsh Government's future funding to councils.","category":"income","matters":"Reported balanced budget masks underlying costs of \u00a310.7m that would be unaffordable without continued uncertain grant funding","figures":"Reported cost \u00a38.678m; pEPR grant \u00a32m used (\u00a32.4m total received); underlying cost without pEPR \u00a310.7m; budget \u00a38.7m","quote":"What is uncertain is how much that funding will be, and whether it impacts in anyway on WG's future funding to Council's in Wales.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-03"},"name":"Denbighshire","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-24","since_iso":"2026-08-25","distress":false,"headline":"First full year (2025/26) balanced budget rests on \u00a32m Extended Producer Responsibility grant described as uncertain","lead":"Reported balanced budget masks underlying costs of \u00a310.7m that would be unaffordable without continued uncertain grant funding","als